<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <style>
        
        * {
            font-family: 'Verdana, sans-serif';
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        
        h1, h2 {
            color: #2c3e50;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            border-bottom: 2px solid #eee;
        }

        
        #main-title {
            background-color: #3498db;
            color: white;
            padding: 15px;
            text-align: center;
        }

        
        .info-box {
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            padding: 10px;
            background-color: #f9f9f9;
            border-left: 5px solid #e67e22;
        }

        
        div span {
            color: #e74c3c;
            font-weight: bold;
            text-decoration: underline;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1 id="main-title">CSS Selector Demonstration</h1>

    <h2>Grouped Heading (H2)</h2>
    <h3>Grouped Heading (H3)</h3>

    <div class="info-box">
        This is a paragraph inside a <strong>class</strong> selector.
    </div>

    <div>
        <p>This is a regular div. Inside here, the <span>descendant selector</span> makes this text red and bold.</p>
    </div>

    <p>This <span>span</span> is NOT inside a div, so it stays normal.</p>

</body>
</html>
